          "content": "**The pixel:** It's a fully transparent pixel (its alpha channel is 0 in the RGBA data). When displayed on a white background — as it is here — it appears **white**.\n\n**The banner:** It shows four translucent, glossy **dice** tumbling in mid-air against a white background:\n\n- A **blue** die (upper left)\n- A **green** die (upper right)\n- A **red** die (centre, the largest and sharpest — showing a 3 on top and a 5 on the front face)\n- A **yellow** die (partially visible beneath the red one)\n\nThe red die is in sharp focus while the others are softly blurred, giving the impression of dice captured mid-roll. This kind of image is often used as a placeholder or \"default\" graphic, much like the transparent pixel itself.",
